// A lobby whose arch shows a window onto a gallery of screens, each showing one of the gallery's own sources: its
// cabinet's picture, its own text in its own font, and a view through its own camera of a green lamp no seat looking
// on along the walk sees. A seat walks through the arch into the gallery, where the same screens bind for the seat
// presented there. Staging relocates the gallery's cartridge and font beside its staged document.

schema: "puck.world.definition.v1"

import "rooms.puck"

entry world lobby = lobby(there: "gallery", nesting: 3)
world gallery = gallery(nesting: 3)
